        <!-- Column headings the bank statement importer should recognise on
             sight.  base_import keeps these in `base_import.mapping` and
             normally only learns them after a first successful import, so the
             first file an accountant ever uploads arrives unmapped - which is
             how "Debet" ends up on Journal Items / Debit and every row fails
             as unbalanced.  Seeding them means the first file is already
             matched.

             Looked up as `header.lower()`, so every column_name is lowercase.

             The counterparty column goes to `partner_name`, the plain text
             field, and NOT to partner_id: a name the database has never seen
             blocks the whole import with "No matching record found", and a
             bank statement is full of names that are not contacts yet.  Odoo
             reads partner_name when it suggests a partner during matching, so
             nothing is lost. -->

